(## System Overview) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(The project retrieves Patient, Condition, Observation, and Encounter resources from a) Tj
0 -12 Td
(FHIR R4 server. `fhir_retriever.py` pseudonymizes identifiers and dates, stores) Tj
0 -12 Td
(normalized fields in SQLite, exports CSV files, and maintains a restartable JSON cache.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(`fhir_api.py` exposes the stored data through FastAPI. `fhir_analyse.py` calculates) Tj
0 -12 Td
(descriptive statistics for numeric Observations. `etl.py` assembles retrieval and) Tj
0 -12 Td
(analysis for Docker. The remaining modules are focused tests, and) Tj
0 -12 Td
(`generate_documentation_pdf.py` creates this documentation.) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(## Data and Execution Flow) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(1. The retriever requests paginated FHIR Bundles.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(2. Resources are copied, identifiers are replaced with deterministic HMAC pseudonyms,) Tj
0 -12 Td
(and patient-linked dates are shifted.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(3. `FHIRDatabase` stores normalized columns in `fhir_resources.sqlite3`; it migrates) Tj
0 -12 Td
(older `resource_json` schemas when encountered.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(4. CSV exports and the compressed resource cache are updated for restartability.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(5. FastAPI reads the configured SQLite file directly, while analysis joins normalized) Tj
0 -12 Td
(Observation, Patient, and Encounter columns.) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(## Configuration) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(Set `FHIR_PSEUDONYMIZATION_KEY` before retrieval. Local output defaults to) Tj
0 -12 Td
(`fhir_output/fhir_resources.sqlite3`; Docker uses `/data/fhir_resources.sqlite3`. The) Tj
0 -12 Td
(older `data/fhir.sqlite3` file is not referenced by the application.) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
